1
00:00:00,345 --> 00:00:02,404
Coca-Cola tested its new formula on

2
00:00:02,414 --> 00:00:04,736
about two hundred thousand people.

3
00:00:04,810 --> 00:00:05,859
They loved it.

4
00:00:06,054 --> 00:00:08,549
Seventy-nine days later, it was gone.

5
00:00:08,727 --> 00:00:10,118
1985.

6
00:00:10,175 --> 00:00:12,118
Pepsi is beating Coke in blind taste

7
00:00:12,175 --> 00:00:12,679
tests.

8
00:00:12,831 --> 00:00:14,821
So Coke changes its ninety-nine-year-old

9
00:00:14,831 --> 00:00:15,671
recipe.

10
00:00:15,745 --> 00:00:16,550
Sweeter.

11
00:00:16,624 --> 00:00:17,386
Smoother.

12
00:00:17,469 --> 00:00:20,067
In blind tests, it beats old Coke.

13
00:00:20,141 --> 00:00:21,069
And Pepsi.

14
00:00:21,264 --> 00:00:22,655
New Coke launches.

15
00:00:22,712 --> 00:00:23,828
And America...

16
00:00:23,902 --> 00:00:24,758
loses it.

17
00:00:24,909 --> 00:00:27,577
Fifteen hundred angry calls a day.

18
00:00:27,651 --> 00:00:29,775
One letter was addressed to Chief Dodo.

19
00:00:29,944 --> 00:00:31,899
Coke hired a psychiatrist to listen

20
00:00:31,909 --> 00:00:32,439
in.

21
00:00:32,513 --> 00:00:34,387
Callers sounded like they were grieving.

22
00:00:34,625 --> 00:00:36,960
So how did two hundred thousand tests

23
00:00:36,970 --> 00:00:38,307
get it so wrong?

24
00:00:38,476 --> 00:00:39,798
They were sips.

25
00:00:39,855 --> 00:00:42,121
And in a single sip, the sweeter drink

26
00:00:42,131 --> 00:00:43,083
tends to win.

27
00:00:43,157 --> 00:00:44,893
But nobody drinks a sip.

28
00:00:44,950 --> 00:00:46,482
You drink the whole can.

29
00:00:46,642 --> 00:00:48,356
The original came back as Coca-Cola

30
00:00:48,366 --> 00:00:50,356
Classic, and was soon beating Pepsi

31
00:00:50,366 --> 00:00:50,930
again.

32
00:00:51,122 --> 00:00:52,478
Was it all a plan?

33
00:00:52,553 --> 00:00:54,439
Coke's president said: we're not that

34
00:00:54,449 --> 00:00:55,163
dumb...

35
00:00:55,173 --> 00:00:56,555
and we're not that smart.

